message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below. The paper will be the preferred citation once it is released."
title: "chipledger: an accounting identity for AI-accelerator performance growth, 2012–2026"
abstract: >-
  Is Huang's law Moore's law? A sourced dataset of data-centre AI accelerators and an exact
  per-chip accounting identity that splits the growth of headline throughput into transistor
  density, die area, clock, architectural specialization and numeric precision, with an
  uncertainty for every share. Code: MIT. Data: CC-BY-4.0.
type: software
